{
 "total": 39.4,
 "segs": [
  {
   "text": "Why don't we just fill a rocket with our trash and dump it in the Sun?",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 3.72
  },
  {
   "text": "The Sun is huge. Hard to miss.",
   "start": 4.27,
   "end": 7.79
  },
  {
   "text": "But Earth moves sideways at thirty kilometers a second, and the rocket keeps that speed.",
   "start": 8.29,
   "end": 14.174
  },
  {
   "text": "So it misses, and circles the Sun.",
   "start": 14.474,
   "end": 17.024
  },
  {
   "text": "To actually hit it, you have to cancel that speed. That takes fifty-five times more energy than going to Mars.",
   "start": 17.574,
   "end": 26.345
  },
  {
   "text": "And we make over two billion tonnes of trash a year. That's at least eighty million full rockets. Every year.",
   "start": 26.845,
   "end": 36.065
  },
  {
   "text": "So, recycle.",
   "start": 36.815,
   "end": 38.902
  }
 ],
